@@ -518,6 +518,33 @@ Do not call for: assigning to someone not on the map's team; assigning a non-wor
 Assignees must be current owners, admins, or members of the map's team. Archived maps: can still change assignee.
 
 Examples: "Assign to Carol" → mindmap_work_assign(node_id="...", assignee_id="<carol-uuid>"). "Unassign this" → mindmap_work_assign(node_id="...", assignee_id=null).""",
+    "memsys_workflow_set": """Define (create-or-replace) this team's work-item workflow — the set of statuses a work item can be in and which (from → to) transitions are allowed, with an optional reason requirement per edge.
+
+Call when: the team wants a custom status pipeline instead of the built-in one (e.g. backlog / in_review / qa / shipped); an admin is configuring task-tracking for their team. When no workflow is set the built-in pipeline (todo / in_progress / blocked / done / cancelled) applies.
+
+Do not call for: teams you don't administer; status values used by an in-progress work item that aren't in your workflow (those items must be transitioned out of unknown statuses first).
+
+statuses is the ordered, unique set of valid statuses; initial_status (required to be one of them) is the status a newly-marked work item starts at. Each transition's from_status and to_status must be in statuses; from_status == to_status (self-loops) is rejected. Setting replaces any existing workflow for the team.
+
+Examples: "Use a Kanban pipeline" → memsys_workflow_set(team_id="...", name="kanban", statuses=["backlog","ready","in_progress","in_review","qa","shipped"], initial_status="backlog", transitions=[{from:"backlog",to:"ready"},{from:"ready",to:"in_progress"},{from:"in_progress",to:"in_review"},{from:"in_review",to:"qa"},{from:"qa",to:"shipped"},{from:"qa",to:"in_progress",reason_required:true}]).""",
+    "memsys_workflow_get": """Read a team's work-item workflow (statuses, initial status, and allowed transitions).
+
+Call when: you need to know which status values and transitions a team's work items accept; deciding what statuses to offer in a UI; diagnosing a status-change rejection.
+
+Do not call for: teams you are not a member of (the call returns nothing for non-members, indistinguishable from "no workflow configured").
+
+Returns null when the team has no custom workflow configured, in which case memsys_mark_work_item / memsys_work_set_status use the built-in pipeline (todo / in_progress / blocked / done / cancelled).
+
+Example: memsys_workflow_get(team_id="...").""",
+    "memsys_workflow_delete": """Remove a team's custom work-item workflow so it reverts to the built-in pipeline.
+
+Call when: an admin wants to undo a custom workflow and return the team to the default status pipeline.
+
+Do not call for: teams you don't administer.
+
+The deletion cascades to the workflow's transitions. Existing work items keep their current status but must thereafter use the built-in transitions.
+
+Example: memsys_workflow_delete(team_id="...").""",
     "memsys_admin_find_user": """Search every user on the instance by partial email address or display name. Operator tool — requires the system.manage_tenants permission, which only a system_admin holds.
 
 Call when: the user needs a tenant_id they do not have ("what's Manasi's user id?"); you are about to add someone to a team and need to confirm which account is theirs; the user asks who signed up recently, or how many accounts exist matching some name or domain.
